course: dictionary
lesson: 15450
title: Sterile: clean, or cold and empty?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sterile has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one. «The nurse opened a sterile bandage.» Here sterile means completely clean, with no germs at all.
explain: The same word can describe a place or an idea: «The new office felt sterile, with grey walls and no pictures.» Here sterile means dull and lifeless, with no warmth. Ask yourself: is the sentence about germs, about growing things, or about feelings?
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence and read it again. Is the bandage free from germs? Yes, that makes sense. Can the sterile field grow crops? No, so the field must be unable to grow anything.
fact: Sterile is an adjective, a word that describes a noun.
fact: «Sterile» means completely clean and free from germs, like «sterile water» in a hospital.
fact: «Sterile» can also mean unable to have babies or young, or, for plants, unable to make seeds or fruit.
fact: «Sterile» land cannot grow crops, and a «sterile» room or argument feels dull, lifeless and without warmth or new ideas.
fact: In science and health lessons, sterile means no living germs, so sterile tools are safe to use on a wound.
exercise: The nurse put a «sterile dressing» on the cut. What does sterile mean here? | *Completely clean, free from germs | Cold and empty | Unable to grow crops | Dull and boring
exercise: «The farmer said the field was sterile, so nothing would grow there.» What does sterile mean? | Full of colourful flowers | Full of germs | *Unable to grow crops | Very wet and muddy
exercise: «The office felt sterile.» What does sterile suggest about the office? | Full of plants | Full of germs | *Dull and lifeless, with no warmth | Very clean and happy
test: «The surgeon used sterile water to clean the wound.» What does sterile mean? | Full of germs | *Free from germs | Warm and wet | Slightly dirty
test: Maya says, «The idea was sterile, with no new thoughts at all.» What does she mean? | *It had no new ideas and no life in it | It was very clean | It grew into a big plant | It was full of colours
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The doctor kept the instruments sterile before the operation»? | *Free from germs | Covered in mud | Made of wood | Unable to make seeds
